Union-query Attack
Attack Principle: Use UNION operator to merge malicious query results into the original query
Feature Detection:
UNION keywords:
UNION, UNION ALL, UNION SELECT
Column count matching techniques:
NULL padding: UNION SELECT NULL, NULL, NULL
Number padding: UNION SELECT 1,2,3,4
Data merging functions (used to compress multiple rows into a single column):
GROUP_CONCAT(...): merge multiple rows into a single string
CONCAT(...), CONCAT_WS(...): concatenate multiple fields
Querying system information:
SELECT queries system tables or system variables after UNION
Querying tables and fields unrelated to business
Judgment Points:
Whether UNION usage conforms to business logic
Whether content queried after UNION is related to the original query
Whether deliberate column count matching behavior exists